  digits 24..72 form a complete residue system mod 49, so every n >= 42 has exactly one numeral; adding a node is
  the odometer d -> d + 1, carrying 72 -> 24 into the next place (since 49 m + 72 + 1 = 49 (m + 1) + 24)
  constructive: ninja_numeration_replay_20261031.py applies session124's 49 digit operators to the new pairs
